  "aiContextParagraph": "The Australian cricket team remains embroiled in a public discourse regarding the 2018 ball-tampering scandal, commonly referred to as Sandpapergate. Following comments made by Usman Khawaja, both he and David Warner were removed from their roles as commentators. While Cricket Australia has provided unanimous support for Pat Cummins to remain as Test captain, recent reports indicate deepening internal friction. Khawaja recently disclosed that he attempted to mediate the conflict by offering a peace proposal to Cricket Australia CEO Todd Greenberg. Simultaneously, former players like Matthew Hayden have advocated for a new investigation into the 2018 events. The situation has prompted widespread commentary from international sports figures, with the focus largely centered on team leadership and the management of the fallout from the original incident.",
